{; Unit: retained Datahike temporal indices for this operator-root store.
 ; Provenance: owner ruling 2026-08-03. Ordinary/user roots retain history;
 ; isolated scratch and eval roots may explicitly choose false at creation.
 :seon.config.db/keep-history? true

 ; Unit: queued compute submissions.
 ; Provenance: core.async.flow alpha3 uses a fixed buffer of 10 per channel;
 ; the scheduling testbed preserved it because a full channel parks the
 ; submitter and loses no work.
 :seon.config.flow.compute/queue-depth 10

 ; This symbolic decision is resolved by the manifest compiler to the machine's
 ; available processors — because a shipped literal is only ever right
 ; on the machine that shipped it. A manifest may override with an
 ; explicit integer. (Calibration context: 2026-07-25 measured 18 cores
 ; here; 22 concurrent evals queued 4 with 71 ms max wait.)
 :seon.config.flow.compute/concurrency :seon.config/available-processors

 ; Unit: concurrent and queued background IO submissions per cluster.
 ; Virtual threads make blocking cheap; these bounds instead limit remote
 ; pressure and durable receipts awaiting settlement.
 :seon.config.flow.io/concurrency 64
 :seon.config.flow.io/queue-depth 64

 ; Unit: foreground capability milliseconds before the volatile context tail
 ; recommends explicit background execution on a later call.
 :seon.config.effect/long-call-ms 2000

 ; Unit: milliseconds allowed for one Flow ping response. Provenance: F1
 ; measured parked mailbox and turn replies in microseconds; 20 ms leaves
 ; orders of magnitude of scheduling room. A missing reply is reported as
 ; unknown, never converted into a healthy observation.
 :seon.config.flow/ping-timeout-ms 20

 ; The eval result caps: how much of an agent value `seon.sci.admit`
 ; projects into a receipt's result-edn. Units below; provenance: the
 ; 2026-08-01 measurements in tmp/admission-caps-2026-08-01/. Wide values
 ; cross 10 ms around 7k nodes, the recursive walk overflows near depth
 ; 5000, and string projection is effectively free; these decisions admit
 ; useful query results while remaining far below the measured cliffs.
 ; Unit: nesting levels.
 :seon.config.eval.result/max-depth 64
 ; Unit: elements retained per collection.
 :seon.config.eval.result/max-collection 8192
 ; Unit: characters retained per string.
 :seon.config.eval.result/max-string 262144
 ; Unit: total nodes visited across the whole projection.
 :seon.config.eval.result/max-nodes 65536

 ; Unit: serialized result-edn characters. Provenance: DERIVED 2026-08-03
 ; as the latency/object floor over the validated 198-sample workload.
 ; At ~476 characters, two N=50 runs took 428.70–462.45 ms with threshold
 ; 343 (50 blob writes) versus 1.11–1.69 ms with 4,096 (all inline). The
 ; archive would mint 557 distinct blob objects at 343 versus 291 at 4,096
 ; while GC still has no effective cutoff. Eligible results also compare the
 ; REAL stored shapes — 4R inline versus 743 + 4W + R for the window,
 ; digest/size envelope, and blob — so this floor never forces a larger row.
 :seon.config.eval.result/blob-threshold 4096

 ; The generic value face is fitted after admission and recursive producer
 ; selection. Its visible budget is estimated tokens; its other bounds are
 ; structural, and its blob threshold reuses the storage decision above.
 ; Unit: estimated tokens (`seon.ai.tokens/estimate`).
 :seon.config.render.agent/token-budget 1024
 ; Unit: nested structural nodes retained in the visible face.
 :seon.config.render.agent/max-depth 8
 ; Unit: children retained per collection node.
 :seon.config.render.agent/max-children 32
 ; Composition is a presentation decision, not another size limit.
 :seon.config.render.agent/composition :multiline

 ; Unit: retained entries in one routed `/data` window; the navigation
 ; elision marker rides beside them, never inside the count (the
 ; 2026-08-01 off-by-one repair). Provenance: the 2026-08-01 cap measurements
 ; raised admission width to runaway-query scale; presentation remains at the
 ; structural renderer's proven readable default and must not inherit it.
 :seon.render.value/max-collection 8

 ; Unit: collection entries printed before the `...` marker. Provenance:
 ; the surviving JVM printer used 32 while keeping structural `/data`
 ; navigation at 8; this is the ordinary REPL face, not an admission cap.
 :seon.print/length 32

 ; Unit: nested collection levels printed before the `#` marker. Provenance:
 ; the surviving JVM printer used 8 to keep accidental recursive values
 ; readable while leaving normal result shapes intact.
 :seon.print/level 8

 ; Unit: milliseconds of wall clock per agent evaluation.
 ; Provenance: the ONLY limit sci has — it counts no steps, so this is
 ; the whole bound on an interpreted form (reference-code/sci/doc/
 ; interrupt.md:23-35). Calibrated against the measured shapes rather
 ; than a feeling: an authored infinite loop dies at ~55 ms once the
 ; flag flips, and the suite's runaway cases stop inside 300 ms, so a
 ; 30 s ceiling is three orders of magnitude above the mechanism's
 ; latency and still bounded well below a human's patience. It bounds
 ; INTERPRETED work only: a form blocked inside a host call never
 ; enters an interpreted body and is covered by the caller's submission
 ; backstop and the process boundary, never by this.
 :seon.config.eval/time-limit-ms 30000

 ; THE FILESYSTEM CAPABILITY. These are policy facts shared by every agent,
 ; never per-agent grants. Relative request paths resolve against the explicit
 ; working root; the process working directory is not an undeclared fallback.
 ; Provenance: the 2026-08-03 tracked-tree census found 2,793 first-party
 ; src/test/resources/docs/config files, maximum depth 9, and a largest tracked
 ; file of 2,327,591 bytes. The scan/write ceilings are ~7x that observed file;
 ; the traversal ceiling is >23x the observed first-party entry count; depth is
 ; >7x observed. The 8,192-byte inline window matches the standing admitted
 ; collection ceiling so byte-vector reads cannot be clipped after dispatch.
 :seon.config.fs/working-root "."
 :seon.config.fs/roots ["."]
 ; Unit: bytes streamed through one complete read/digest pass.
 :seon.config.fs/max-read-bytes 16777216
 ; Unit: bytes retained in one returned read window.
 :seon.config.fs/max-inline-bytes 8192
 ; Unit: bytes accepted for one conditional write.
 :seon.config.fs/max-write-bytes 16777216
 ; Unit: matched paths returned by one glob.
 :seon.config.fs/max-glob-results 4096
 ; Unit: directory entries examined by one glob.
 :seon.config.fs/max-traversal-entries 65536
 ; Unit: directory edges descended by one glob.
 :seon.config.fs/max-depth 64

 ; THE FOREGROUND SHELL CAPABILITY. Completion is observed from Process.onExit;
 ; the time limit is only the legitimate foreign-process backstop. The 30 s /
 ; 1 s pair retains the measured JVM/Bun quarry policy recorded in the timeout
 ; census. Inline output reuses the 4,096-byte measured blob crossover; preview
 ; is one quarter of that complete evidence window. Stdin matches the measured
 ; largest-file filesystem ceiling, so composing a file into a child requires
 ; no smaller unexplained bound. PATH/HOME/LANG are explicitly absent optional
 ; overrides: the child inherits every parent variable, and a declared value
 ; replaces only its named variable.
 ; Unit: milliseconds until the foreign-process backstop fires.
 :seon.config.shell/time-limit-ms 30000
 ; Unit: milliseconds between polite and forced exact-tree termination.
 :seon.config.shell/termination-grace-ms 1000
 ; Unit: complete stdout or stderr bytes returned inline.
 :seon.config.shell/inline-output-bytes 4096
 ; Unit: UTF-8 prefix bytes attempted for blob-backed output evidence.
 :seon.config.shell/preview-bytes 1024
 ; Unit: bytes accepted on one child stdin stream.
 :seon.config.shell/stdin-max-bytes 16777216
 :seon.config.shell/path :seon.config/absent
 :seon.config.shell/home :seon.config/absent
 :seon.config.shell/lang :seon.config/absent

 ; Unit: count of same-signature faults since this process started.
 ; Provenance: the second escalation condition (the first is "no
 ; attributable agent"). Three says a fault that happened once was
 ; noise, twice was bad luck, and three times is a pattern the
 ; escalation owner must hear about. Counted by query over committed
 ; facts; there is no stored tally to drift.
 :seon.config.error/recurrence-limit 3

 ; Unit: agent-to-agent hops in ONE causal chain, counted back through
 ; committed transaction metadata to the last message that came from
 ; outside the agent population.
 ; Provenance: the quarry shipped 8 (`seon.warn/hop-cap`,
 ; src-old/seon/agent/message.cljc:316) and its scar is recorded — a
 ; GLOBAL newest-inbound count summed every wake-chain hop, so a routine
 ; two-round delegation (parent→A→parent→B→parent) hit the cap and
 ; silently deadlocked, and the fix was a per-peer count with a
 ; human-message barrier. This chain walk is that fix arrived at
 ; structurally instead: the barrier is free, because a message from
 ; outside the population has no triggering transaction to walk back
 ; through and therefore starts at zero by construction. 16 is that
 ; hard-won 8 doubled, on the reasoning that the quarry's number was
 ; calibrated against a count that OVERSTATED depth: eight rounds of
 ; unattended ping-pong is a runaway, four is a conversation, and the
 ; cost of being wrong low is a delegation that dies mid-thought.
 :seon.config.message/max-chain 16

 ; Unit: consecutive runs per idle→running episode — runs since (and
 ; including) the one answering the last OUTSIDE trigger, derived
 ; purely from committed facts (~34 µs on a 64-run history; no stored
 ; counter, and an outside trigger's own run IS the reset).
 ; Provenance: the F1 agent-graph contract
 ; (docs/prds/sci-execution-runtime/plan/
 ; f1-agent-graph-contracts-2026-07-28.md §7) and the owner ruling of
 ; 2026-07-28 setting the shipped value at 100: the dial bounds
 ; LEGITIMATE self-continuation, never a loop bug (any loop is a design
 ; defect to dissolve), so it sits well above the deepest observed
 ; useful chain while still ending an unattended runaway within one
 ; sitting. When the dial is hit, deferred agent-sent triggers stay
 ; conserved unanswered rows and the next outside trigger opens
 ; normally — nothing is dropped and nothing is written.
 :seon.config.run/max-episode-runs 100

 ; WHO hears what nobody else can be told about. It names the root agent
 ; because boot now SEEDS one — the reason this was absent when the dial
 ; landed was that a default naming an agent that may not exist would be
 ; a lie, and that is no longer the case: every cluster has a root from
 ; its first transaction, free, with no process and no tokens.
 ; The dial stays OPTIONAL in the shape, and that is not vestigial —
 ; a manifest may override it to absent, and absence still means the
 ; error fact is committed with no escalation message. `commit-tx` also
 ; refuses to address an agent this cluster does not have, so a dial
 ; pointing at a typo costs the message, never the record.
 :seon.config.error/escalate-to "root"

 ; Unit: categorical core-fault disposition.
 ; Provenance: the 2026-07-27 error ruling requires development to fail
 ; loudly and production to degrade only by explicit configuration.
 :seon.config/on-core-error :panic

 ; THE DISK GOVERNOR OBSERVES AND REPORTS; IT NEVER QUOTAS WORK. The warning
 ; boundary is crossed when either absolute or proportional usable space is
 ; low. Provenance: disk-burn-forensics-2026-08-04.md found 144 GiB consumed
 ; by project-owned trees and established 50 GiB / 10% as the operator warning
 ; thresholds. Production logs and continues; the development `:panic` policy
 ; stops the boot after recording the warning so low-space incidents cannot be
 ; silently normalized. Neither path imposes a runtime quota.
 ; Unit: usable bytes on the managed root's filesystem.
 :seon.config.maintenance/min-usable-bytes 53687091200
 ; Unit: usable / total filesystem bytes.
 :seon.config.maintenance/min-usable-ratio 0.10
 ; Unit: bytes retained in the live log inode before rotation. The same
 ; forensics pass found one unbounded 965 MiB log; 64 MiB preserves extensive
 ; boot/runtime evidence while bounding one cluster's active file.
 :seon.config.maintenance/log-max-bytes 67108864
 ; Unit: prior bounded log files retained beside the live inode.
 :seon.config.maintenance/log-retained-files 4

 ; THE OPERATOR WAITS ON EVENTS, NEVER A FLAT OPERATION CLOCK. This is the
 ; one last-resort silence circuit breaker for a boot phase, prepl connect or
 ; response, exact-process exit after SIGTERM, or the detached adoption gate.
 ; Every observed event starts a fresh interval. Firing names the silent event
 ; and this governing fact; it is a bug report, never successful completion.
 ; Provenance: P19 measured 11 s for dependency namespace loading and 2.6 s
 ; for the remaining boot tower, while the former flat 30 s readiness deadline
 ; abandoned a live JVM during unrelated filesystem work. Thirty seconds keeps
 ; the measured legitimate phase intact while bounding absent foreign events.
 ; Unit: milliseconds without the next declared operator event.
 :seon.config.operator/event-silence-backstop-ms 30000

 ; THE VIEW'S PORT IS EXPLICITLY ABSENT, and absence is the state: with
 ; no dial the port is DERIVED from the cluster name (7700-7999, FNV-1a
 ; over the name — `seon.render.web/derived-port`), so every named
 ; cluster is bookmarkable and answers on the same port after every
 ; restart. Setting this pins one instead, and an explicit port is
 ; somebody's decision that outranks a derivation.
 ; Unit: TCP port. A derived port that is already taken falls back to an
 ; ephemeral one and reports BOTH numbers.
 :seon.config.web/port :seon.config/absent

 ; my.web ceilings. PROVENANCE: these are UNCALIBRATED starting points
 ; chosen to match the measured filesystem ceilings (16 MiB read, 8 KiB
 ; inline window) so one family's limits do not silently contradict
 ; another's; they ship because a declared dial without a default
 ; refuses every cluster start, not because anything measured them.
 ; Calibrate against real fetches and record the numbers.
 ; Unit: bytes streamed through one complete response read.
 :seon.config.web/max-response-bytes 16777216
 ; Unit: bytes retained inline before the body rides the blob tier.
 :seon.config.web/max-inline-bytes 8192
 ; Unit: redirect hops followed before one fetch refuses.
 :seon.config.web/max-redirects 5
 ; Unit: milliseconds for one outbound request. A remote host is
 ; genuinely unobservable, so this deadline is a legitimate backstop.
 :seon.config.web/timeout-ms 30000
 ; Unit: result rows returned by one search.
 :seon.config.web/max-search-results 10
 ; The search provider is a config fact, never a provider-shaped API.
 ; Verified live 2026-08-03: research/serper-probe-2026-08-03.md.
 :seon.config.web/search-endpoint "https://google.serper.dev/search"
 :seon.config.web/search-api-key-variable "SERPER_API_KEY"
 :seon.config.web/search-result-projection seon.web.search/organic-results

 ; Unit: milliseconds between repaints of one tab. Provenance: 16 ms is
 ; one frame at 60 fps, the owner's stated bar, and it is a FLOOR rather
 ; than a tick — a burst of commits inside one window costs one repaint
 ; and a quiet cluster costs none.
 :seon.config.render/coalesce-ms 16

 ; THE MODEL SEAM. DeepSeek is the standing default provider; each :call
 ; resolves current facts, so the provider is a fact rather than a literal in
 ; a drive script. Nothing here spends anything: an installed loop with no
 ; trigger makes no call.
 ; Unit: absolute URL of one OpenAI-compatible completions endpoint.
 :seon.config.ai/endpoint "https://api.deepseek.com/chat/completions"

 ; Unit: the provider's own model name. Provenance: owner ruling
 ; 2026-08-01 — deepseek-v4-flash (version DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731, released 2026-07-31) is the
 ; default: 1M context, 384K max output, thinking default-on, 5x the
 ; concurrency at ~1/3 the output price of v4-pro. Thinking/max-token
 ; dials are being calibrated by the flash-bench lane; this row is the
 ; model selection only.
 :seon.config.ai/model "deepseek-v4-flash"

 ; Unit: maximum provider completion tokens, including reasoning tokens.
 ; Provenance: interim 65,536 while flash-bench calibration settles the
 ; optimized non-thinking parameter set required by owner ruling #34.
 ; The former 8,192 default retained the same starvation class already seen
 ; at 4,096, so the live default must carry ample reasoning + reply headroom.
 :seon.config.ai/max-tokens 65536

 ; Explicitly disabled by owner ruling #34: ordinary per-turn agents optimize
 ; for reasonably smart, fast, and cheap work; planners opt into thinking with
 ; an agent-entity override. The flash-quality-interrogation-2026-08-01 bench
 ; measured 9.8 s non-thinking versus 21.3 s thinking-high median ($0.0003
 ; versus $0.0007 off-peak).
 :seon.config.ai/thinking :disabled

 ; The optional request controls inherit provider behavior until the flash
 ; calibration provides an evidence-backed shipped value. Explicit absence is
 ; a decision and never becomes a stored nil.
 :seon.config.ai/temperature :seon.config/absent
 :seon.config.ai/top-p :seon.config/absent
 :seon.config.ai/frequency-penalty :seon.config/absent
 :seon.config.ai/presence-penalty :seon.config/absent
 :seon.config.ai/stop :seon.config/absent
 :seon.config.ai/response-format :seon.config/absent
 :seon.config.ai/extra-body-edn :seon.config/absent

 ; Unit: the NAME of an environment variable. Never the credential —
 ; the key is read at the leaf, never becomes a datom, never enters Git.
 :seon.config.ai/api-key-variable "DEEPSEEK_API_KEY"

 ; Authentication is credential-backed by default, so the mutually exclusive
 ; literal no-auth fact is explicitly absent.
 :seon.config.ai/no-auth :seon.config/absent

 ; Unit: milliseconds. Provenance: DeepSeek V4 Flash calibration report
 ; (commit a73d928bf): Flash thinking-high reached 103.817 s and Pro reached
 ; 108.783 s, so 60,000 rejects successful calls and 120,000 leaves little
 ; stochastic headroom. This is a deadline on unobservable remote HTTP state,
 ; not an internal readiness clock.
 :seon.config.ai/timeout-ms 180000

 ; THE BACKUP DESCRIPTOR ROW IS EXPLICITLY ABSENT. A shipped backup
 ; would be a second provider this repository picked for everybody, and
 ; the honest default is "one target, no failover": with no
 ; :seon.config.ai.backup/model, `disposition` never returns
 ; :failover-now and the no-backup path below is the only resilience
 ; there is. A cluster that wants failover sets ONE dial when the backup
 ; is another model at the same provider, or three more when it is not.
 ; Absence is the state; there is no nil to read.
 :seon.config.ai.backup/model :seon.config/absent
 :seon.config.ai.backup/endpoint :seon.config/absent
 :seon.config.ai.backup/api-key-variable :seon.config/absent
 :seon.config.ai.backup/timeout-ms :seon.config/absent

 ; THE BACKOFF STRATEGY, and it runs on exactly one path: a
 ; conclusively UNPAID transient failure with no backup configured.
 ; Nothing here can re-call a transmitted request — `seon.ai/disposition`
 ; returns :backoff for exactly three error classes, and a request that
 ; may have cost money is not one of them.
 ;
 ; Unit: milliseconds before the first retry.
 ; Provenance: DeepSeek's live plan replies measured 2.7 s, so a first
 ; wait shorter than a second would re-ask a busy provider inside its
 ; own service time; 500 ms is half of that floor and the smallest wait
 ; that is not effectively "immediately".
 :seon.config.ai.retry/base-delay-ms 500

 ; Unit: dimensionless growth factor per retry.
 ; Provenance: doubling is the standard exponential backoff shape and is
 ; what `again`'s multiplicative-strategy composes; anything gentler
 ; makes the retry count the bound instead of the wait.
 :seon.config.ai.retry/multiplier 2.0

 ; Unit: fraction of each delay applied as random spread.
 ; Provenance: jitter exists so N clusters retrying one outage do not
 ; re-synchronize; a quarter of the delay decorrelates them without
 ; making the schedule unrecognizable to somebody reading the log.
 :seon.config.ai.retry/jitter-fraction 0.25

 ; Unit: milliseconds; the cap on any single wait.
 :seon.config.ai.retry/maximum-delay-ms 4000

 ; Unit: count of retries after the first attempt.
 ; Provenance: a rate limit or a 503 either clears in seconds or is an
 ; outage; two retries distinguishes those two cases and a third only
 ; delays telling the agent.
 :seon.config.ai.retry/maximum-retries 2

 ; Unit: milliseconds of TOTAL waiting across all retries.
 ; Provenance: THE BINDING BOUND, and it is bound by responsiveness,
 ; not by patience. (It was originally sized against the 60 s run
 ; lease; leases are DELETED — custody is presence, 2026-07-28 — and
 ; the number survives on its own merits.) The model call itself may
 ; take the full 60 s deadline, so the waiting budget has to stay small
 ; against the one deadline a turn already carries; three seconds
 ; covers the base + one doubled wait without making a backed-off turn
 ; feel wedged.
 :seon.config.ai.retry/maximum-total-delay-ms 3000

 ; DECLARED INITIALIZATION ROWS. Provider wire facts live only on provider
 ; descriptor rows; model rows point to them and carry only model facts.
 :seon.config/initialization
 [{:seon.ai.model/provider-id "deepseek"
   :seon.config.ai/endpoint "https://api.deepseek.com/chat/completions"
   :seon.config.ai/api-key-variable "DEEPSEEK_API_KEY"
   :seon.ai.model/openai-chat-completions true
   :seon.ai.model/output-token-wire-key "max_tokens"}

  {:seon.ai.model/provider-id "moonshot"
   :seon.config.ai/endpoint "https://api.moonshot.ai/v1/chat/completions"
   :seon.config.ai/api-key-variable "MOONSHOT_API_KEY"
   :seon.ai.model/openai-chat-completions true
   :seon.ai.model/output-token-wire-key "max_completion_tokens"}

  {:seon.ai.model/provider-id "meta"
   :seon.config.ai/endpoint "https://api.meta.ai/v1/chat/completions"
   :seon.config.ai/api-key-variable "META_MODEL_API_KEY"
   :seon.ai.model/openai-chat-completions true
   :seon.ai.model/output-token-wire-key "max_tokens"}

